  ("How much does furnace repair cost in Oshawa?", "Furnace repair in Oshawa is quoted in writing after diagnosis, so the price depends on the part. Ignitors, flame sensors and capacitors sit at the low end, blower motors, inducers and boards cost more, and a new high-efficiency furnace starts at $3,300 installed if replacement is the better choice."),
  ("Do you offer emergency furnace repair in Oshawa?", "Yes. No-heat calls are taken evenings, weekends and holidays, and our regular hours are Monday to Saturday 8 am to 8 pm and Sunday 10 am to 5 pm."),
  ("How soon can you come out for a furnace with no heat in Oshawa?", "We book no-heat calls ahead of routine work and give you a realistic window when you call instead of a promised arrival time. While you wait, keep the thermostat set, keep interior doors open and use a safe electric heater in the room you are in."),
  ("Why does my chimney-vented furnace shut off on windy days?", "Wind off Lake Ontario can push flue gases back down the chimney, and the furnace's spill or pressure switch shuts it down to keep those gases out of the house. The furnace is doing its job, and the fix is usually at the chimney cap, the flue sizing or the draft rather than inside the furnace."),
  ("If I replace my old furnace, does the chimney need a liner?", "Only if a gas water heater will keep venting into the chimney on its own after the new furnace moves to side-wall venting. We price a properly sized liner and a side-wall vented water heater so you can compare both."),
